cassette.
The following primers were used: 5′-
CACC
ATGTATAAAATTGTAGAC-3′ (forward primer; CACC was used for directional cloning) and 5′-TTATTTCTTGCTTAAGTACTC-3′ (reverse primer). The PCR product was cloned into pET200/D-TOPO (Invitrogen), and the construct was subsequently transformed into One-Shot TOP10
E. coli
(Invitrogen). After verifying the DNA sequence, the constructs were transformed into
E. coli
BL21 Star (DE3) (Invitrogen) and expressed.
nfnAB
with an
nfnB
3′ His
