When the concentrations of ethanol, acetate, and butyrate are higher than 1 mM and the free-energy change thus permits the synthesis of more than 1.25 mol of ATP, all that has to happen is that the percentage of reduced ferredoxin reoxidized in the RnfABCDEG-catalyzed reaction is increased and the percentage in the NfnAB-catalyzed reaction is decreased (Fig.
6
